overeating is an unforgivable sin in that the game tells you plainly when
you are full. there at the bottom of the screen is the flag: "Satiated"
which should be understood to mean (conservatively) "don't eat anymore
till you're not so full"! burning off food quickly is rather easy ...
however, choking immediately does seem to be cruel and unusual punishment.
not even a cockatrice kills so quickly, so perhaps you should get a few
moves to induce vomiting thus rectifying the situation.

wait there's more ...

choosing alignment via NETHACKOPTIONS seems okay. This should also be
possible during play without the use of magic armor (perhaps an appropriate
unicorn meal, eating the wrong one is not only bad luck but aggravates
monsters, as well).

choosing your pettype via NETHACKOPTIONS seems reasonable also. an even
wilder idea would be a petchoice option (i.e. petchoice:black dragon)
with some penalties for choosing very mean monsters (i.e. your starting
stats could suffer proportionately as in St:5, Dx:5, In:5, Co:5, Wi:5,
Ch:5). choosing a little dog or kitten (or acid blob, etc.) would
invoke no penalties.

no, wait ...

death by trickery may mean that your dungeon has been built
incorrectly. you should re-compile and twiddle the SECURE and other
related defines (i forget exactly how this works). with these options
properly defined when you (and others) play the game your floors will
appear on disk in the format nnnxxxxxx.ll where nnn is your unique userid,
xxxxxx is the name that you used to enter the game and ll is the number
of the floor. this assumes a unix-type dungeon.

you may wish for an item ...

i wish that patchlevel5 solves more problems than it creates. that
doesn't seem to be true of patchlevel4. even if it takes longer to
release i'd like it to be clean. you may never catch all the errors of
intent (like the infinite wish loopholes) but you shouldn't introduce
flaws (like make dependency loops and funky shops) in released patches.
all in all, thanx for a great game!!!

